# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yaolong Zhang et al. (2021). Physically Motivated Recursively Embedded Atom Neural Networks: Incorporating Local Completeness and Nonlocality.
#   Physical Review Letters. doi:10.1103/physrevlett.127.156002  arXiv:2106.08245v5
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2106.08245v5 (sha256 793cc46930f02b56...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 213 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zhang2021.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the REANN model (introduced here) with its tabulated test
# errors on bulk water: the water-I data set of Cheng et al. for five
# cutoff radii (Table 1) and the water-II data set of Zhang et al. (text).
# The CH4 completeness study (learning curves in Fig. 3 and Fig. S4) and
# the SchNet, EANN and BPNN comparison values (Tables 1, S2) are not
# encoded.

