###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - REANN is introduced as 'a physical adaption of the local descriptor-based EANN model' (Summary; also the description of the T = 0 limit). Recorded in the registry as REANN derived from EANN (new registry method; the EANN method paper is not in the corpus).
# - Network sizes per data set are in Table S1 (water-I: atomic NN 32x16, orbital-coefficient NN 16x16, 33 features; water-II: 512x256x128x64 and 64x32, 60 features). Table S1 lists rc 6.2 A for water-I, while Table 1 varies rc; the architecture of the smaller-cutoff models is not restated, so only rc, T and the initial learning rate are encoded.
# - The CH4 results are learning curves only (Fig. 3, Fig. S4). The SchNet values for water-I in Table S2 may come from models trained by the authors, but the paper does not say so; they are not encoded.
# - No training or inference timing is reported.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zhang2021.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

